# Task FEATURE-002-US-005-T01 — Implement: Scenario summaries

> **DaemonCore coding-agent prompt.** Work type: `feature` · Size: `XS` · Priority: `P2` · Status: `todo`

## Where this fits
- **Epic EPIC-002 — Scenario Presets.** Support reusable, named policy scenarios so users start from a coherent position rather than blank sliders. Provides scenarios.yaml, a validated loader, a UI selector and human-readable summaries.
- **Feature FEATURE-002 — Scenario Presets — implementation.**
- **Story FEATURE-002-US-005 — Scenario summaries.** _As a user, I want a short description of each scenario so I understand its intent._

## Objective
As a user, I want a short description of each scenario so I understand its intent.

## What to do
Implement the capability so that every acceptance criterion below holds. Specifically:
- Summary text renders next to the selector
- Summaries are sourced from scenarios.yaml
- Framing is neutral and caveated (not an endorsement)
Add or update docstrings and any necessary types. Keep the change focused on this story; do not pull in scope from other stories/epics.

## Acceptance criteria (Definition of Done)
- [ ] Summary text renders next to the selector
- [ ] Summaries are sourced from scenarios.yaml
- [ ] Framing is neutral and caveated (not an endorsement)
- [ ] New/updated tests pass and cover the above
- [ ] No regression in the existing `pytest` suite

## Dependencies
None within this story. (Respect cross-epic dependencies of the parent epic.)

## Project conventions
- Target Python 3.13. Use British spelling in all user-facing text.
- Keep the pure model layer (`model/`) free of Streamlit; `app.py` is UI/render only.
- Pin any new runtime deps in `requirements.txt`; test-only deps in `requirements-dev.txt`.
- Write deterministic `pytest` tests; follow the style of `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`.
- Match the surrounding code style. Prefer small, coherent diffs over broad refactors.
- Update `README.md` / `docs/` whenever behaviour changes.

## Guardrails (EPIC-002)
- Presets are inputs to the existing engine — do not change engine maths.
- Validate every preset against the engine's input contract.
- Frame scenarios neutrally; they are not endorsements.
- The scenario loader must have no Streamlit dependency.

## Verification
- `python3 -m py_compile <changed .py files>`
- `python3 -m pytest -q` — all tests pass (add/extend tests for this change).

## Notes
- This simulator is a transparent scenario sandbox, not an official forecast — keep that framing in any user-facing text.
- If requirements are ambiguous or you must change a public interface, stop and flag it rather than guessing.
